cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Evaluating Large Language Models for Edge Persistence Estimation in Temporal Graphs under Partial Observation: code and data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Borchardt"
    given-names: "Albert"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cohen2000/MasterThesis"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Code and frozen results of a Master's thesis. Twelve fully recorded temporal networks are
  sampled with four samplers of equal budget (node sampling, random walk, time truncation,
  event sampling); three large language models, a beta-binomial model and a learned reference
  estimate the share of pairs that interact in at least two of five time windows.
keywords:
  - temporal networks
  - graph sampling
  - random walks
  - persistence
  - large language models
